    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">&quot;The book presents a unique way to discover math through puzzles It connects puzzles with many topics in contemporary math It uses a great, unique, &quot;Talmudic&quot; or associative, methodology It has over 50 puzzles and solutions, many of them original It explains math concepts in a simple and intuitive way It highlights the works of many famous mathematicians, including Lewis Carroll and one of his lesser-known &quot;pillow problems&quot;, illuminating some of the ingenious aspects of the puzzle There&apos;s something in it for everyone: math-lovers (professional and amateurs), historians, puzzlers, kids and adults It&apos;s great for teachers who are looking for new ways to engage kids with math It&apos;s a great way to enhance creative thinking and innovation skills It includes a chapter on extremely relevant, real-life math puzzles from COVID-19&quot;-</marc:subfield>
